Condition to check
if s[current index] == '1' and s[previous index] == '0' 
It is not a valid String

Intuition:-
We need to check if all the 1s in the binary string s form at most one contiguous segment.
My first thought was to iterate through the string and detect if there is any '1' appearing after a '0' has already followed previous 1s.
If such a situation occurs, it means there are multiple segments of 1s.

Approach:-
Start iterating from the second character of the string.
Whenever we find a 1 that is immediately after a 0, return False.
If we finish the iteration without finding such a case, return True.
This ensures that all 1s, if present, are part of a single contiguous segment.

Complexity:-
Time complexity:
O(n)
Space complexity:
O(1)

Code:-
class Solution {
    public boolean checkOnesSegment(String s) {
        return !s.contains("01");
    }
}

-------------------------------------------------------------------

class Solution {
    public boolean checkOnesSegment(String s) {
        char[] c = s.toCharArray();
        for(int i = 1; i < c.length; i++) {
            if(c[i] == '1' && c[i - 1] == '0') return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
